course: dictionary
lesson: 15014
title: Resolve: settle it or decide it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resolve is a word with a few meanings. It can mean to solve or settle a problem, or to decide firmly to do something. As a noun, it means strong determination. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «The argument between Maya and Sam was resolved when they shared the blocks.» The argument ended, so resolved must mean settled. Try the swap: «The argument was settled when they shared the blocks.» It still makes sense.
explain: «Tom resolved to read one book every week.» No problem is solved here. Tom made a firm decision, so resolved means decided firmly. Try the swap: «Tom decided firmly to read one book every week.» That fits too.
fact: Resolve is a verb (resolve, resolves, resolved, resolving) and a noun (resolve).
fact: «Resolve» means to solve or settle a problem, argument or question.
fact: «Resolve» means to decide firmly to do something, as in «She resolved to work harder».
fact: «Resolve» as a noun means strong determination, as in «She showed great resolve».
fact: Clue words: a problem, argument or question near resolve points to settling it; to or a plan near resolve points to deciding.
exercise: «The argument at lunchtime was resolved when the friends said sorry.» What does resolved mean? | Shouted about loudly | Written down in a book | Made even bigger | *Settled, so it was over
exercise: Ella says, «I resolve to practise my violin every day.» What does resolve mean here? | *Decide firmly to do something | Argue loudly | Forget about it | Solve a sum
exercise: «Ben kept climbing the hill, even when his legs ached.» Ben showed great resolve. What does resolve mean here? | A shopping list | A loud noise | A type of bread | *Strong determination, never giving up
test: «The class resolved the problem by taking turns.» What does resolved mean? | Copied | *Solved or settled | Wrote about | Made a mess of
test: «Mum showed real resolve when she trained for the race.» What is resolve in this sentence? | A loud shout | A spoon | *Strong determination | Lost hope
exam: «The team resolved to try again tomorrow.» What does resolved mean here? | Argued loudly | *Decided firmly | Put away for later | Lost the game
